  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As the title says. Using the \"End Length\" or \"End Offset\" options on Dynamic Bone counts towards the dynamic bone limiter, causing your dynamic bones to be turned off. However, these *don't* show up on the performance stats at all, which greatly adds to the confusion.\n\nOn a related note, the root bone in dynamic bone counts toward both transform count and collision check count, even though the root bone never gets processed and should never count.\n\nHappens in build 751 and has happened since the limiter was introduced.",
